  "answer": "Yes. Under section 89 of the Code of Criminal Procedure the Court may restore attached property (or the net proceeds of a sale) to a person who, within two years of the attachment, appears before the Court, shows that he did not abscond or conceal himself to avoid execution of the warrant and was unable to attend the proclamation, and then the property shall be delivered to him after costs are satisfied.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "section": "89",
      "source": "CrPC",
      "quote": "If, within two years from the date of the attachment any person whose property is or has been at the disposal of the Government, under sub-section (7) of section 88, appears voluntarily ... and proves ... that he did not abscond or conceal himself for the purpose of avoiding execution of the warrant, ... such property ... shall, after satisfying thereout all costs incurred in consequence of the attachment, be delivered to him."
